H3600.definition:
a form for H3564 (כּוּר) (only in the dual);
a cooking range (consisting of two parallel stones, across which the boiler is set)
KJV: ranges for pots.

H3601.definition:
from H3787 (כָּשֵׁר); compare H6418 (פֶּלֶךְ)
literally a director, i.e. the spindle or shank of adistaff, by which it is twirled
KJV: spindle.

H3602.definition:
from H3541 (כֹּה);
just so, referring to the previous or following context
KJV: after that (this) manner, this matter, (even) so, in such a case, thus.

H3603.definition:
from H3769 (כָּרַר);
a circle, i.e. (by implication) a circumjacent tract or region, especially the Ghor or valley of the Jordan; also a (round) loaf; also a talent (or large [round] coin)
KJV: loaf, morsel, piece, plain, talent.

H3604.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3603 (כִּכָּר);
a talent
KJV: talent.

H3605.definition:
or (Jeremiah 33:8) כּוֹל; from H3634 (כָּלַל);
properly, the whole; hence, all, any or every (in the singular only, but often in a plural sense)
KJV: (in) all (manner, (ye)), altogether, any (manner), enough, every (one, place, thing), howsoever, as many as, (no-) thing, ought, whatsoever, (the) whole, whoso(-ever).

H3606.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3605 (כֹּל)
{properly, the whole; hence, all, any or every (in the singular only, but often in a plural sense)}
KJV: all, any, + (forasmuch) as, + be-(for this) cause, every, + no (manner, -ne), + there (where) -fore, + though, what (where, who) -soever, (the) whole.

H3607.definition:
a primitive root;
to restrict, by act (hold back or in) or word (prohibit)
KJV: finish, forbid, keep (back), refrain, restrain, retain, shut up, be stayed, withhold.

H3608.definition:
from H3607 (כָּלָא);
a prison
KJV: prison. Compare H3610 (כִּלְאַיִם), H3628 (כְּלִיא).

H3609.definition:
apparently from H3607 (כָּלָא) and H1 (אָב); restraint of (his) father;
Kilab, an Israelite
KJV: Chileab.

H3610.definition:
dual of H3608 (כֶּלֶא) in the original sense of separation;
two heterogeneities
KJV: divers seeds (-e kinds), mingled (seed).

H3611.definition:
from an unused root means. to yelp, or else to attack;
a dog; hence (by euphemism) a male prostitute
KJV: dog.

H3612.definition:
perhaps a form of H3611 (כֶּלֶב), or else from the same root in the sense of forcible;
Caleb, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Caleb.

H3613.definition:
from H3612 (כָּלֵב) and H672 (אֶפְרָת);
Caleb-Ephrathah, a place in Egypt (if the text is correct)
KJV: Caleb-ephrathah.

H3614.definition:
probably by erroneous transcription for כָּלֵבִי; patronymically from H3612 (כָּלֵב);
a Calebite or descendant of Caleb
KJV: of the house of Caleb.

H3615.definition:
a primitive root;
to end, whether intransitive (to cease, be finished, perish) or transitived (to complete, prepare, consume)
KJV: accomplish, cease, consume (away), determine, destroy (utterly), be (when... were) done, (be an) end (of), expire, (cause to) fail, faint, finish, fulfil, [idiom] fully, [idiom] have, leave (off), long, bring to pass, wholly reap, make clean riddance, spend, quite take away, waste.

H3617.definition:
from H3615 (כָּלָה);
a completion; adverb, completely; also destruction
KJV: altogether, (be, utterly) consume(-d), consummation(-ption), was determined, (full, utter) end, riddance.

H3618.definition:
from H3634 (כָּלַל);
a bride (as if perfect); hence, a son's wife
KJV: bride, daughter-in-law, spouse.

H3619.definition:
from the same as H3611 (כֶּלֶב);
a bird-trap (as furnished with a clap-stick or treadle to spring it); hence, a basket (as resembling a wicker cage)
KJV: basket, cage.

H3620.definition:
the same as H3619 (כְּלוּב)xlit kᵉlûb corrected to kᵉlûwb;
Kelub, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Chelub.

H3621.definition:
a form of H3612 (כָּלֵב);
Kelubai, an Israelite
KJV: Chelubai.

H3622.definition:
from H3615 (כָּלָה); completed;
Keluhai, an Israelite
KJV: Chelluh.

H3623.definition:
denominative passive participle from H3618 (כַּלָּה)lemma כַּלָה missing dagesh, corrected to כַּלָּה;
bridehood (only in the plural)
KJV: espousal.

H3624.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be complete;
maturity
KJV: full (old) age.

H3625.definition:
the same as H3624 (כֶּלַח);
Kelach, a place in Assyria
KJV: Calah.

H3626.definition:
from H3605 (כֹּל) and H2374 (חֹזֶה); every seer;
Col-Chozeh, an Israelite
KJV: Col-hozeh.

H3627.definition:
from H3615 (כָּלָה);
something prepared, i.e. any apparatus (as an implement, utensil, dress, vessel or weapon)
KJV: armour(-bearer), artillery, bag, carriage, [phrase] furnish, furniture, instrument, jewel, that is made of, [idiom] one from another, that which pertaineth, pot, [phrase] psaltery, sack, stuff, thing, tool, vessel, ware, weapon, [phrase] whatsoever.

H3628.definition:
or כְּלוּא; from H3627 (כְּלִי) (compare H3608 (כֶּלֶא));
a prison
KJV: prison.

H3629.definition:
feminine of H3627 (כְּלִי) (only in the plural);
a kidney (as an essential organ); figuratively, the mind (as the interior self)
KJV: kidneys, reins.

H3630.definition:
a form of H3631 (כִּלָּיוֹן);
Kiljon, an Israelite
KJV: Chilion.

H3631.definition:
from H3615 (כָּלָה);
pining, destruction
KJV: consumption, failing.

H3632.definition:
from H3634 (כָּלַל);
complete; as noun, the whole (specifically, a sacrifice entirely consumed); as adverb, fully
KJV: all, every whit, flame, perfect(-ion), utterly, whole burnt offering (sacrifice), wholly.

H3633.definition:
from H3557 (כּוּל); sustenance;
Calcol, an Israelite
KJV: Calcol, Chalcol.

H3634.definition:
a primitive root;
to complete
KJV: (make) perfect.

H3635.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3634 (כָּלַל);
to complete
KJV: finish, make (set) up.

H3636.definition:
from H3634 (כָּלַל); complete;
Kelal, an Israelite
KJV: Chelal.

H3637.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to wound; but only figuratively, to taunt or insult
KJV: be (make) ashamed, blush, be confounded, be put to confusion, hurt, reproach, (do, put to) shame.

H3638.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Kilmad, a place apparently in the Assyrian empire
KJV: Chilmad.

H3639.definition:
from H3637 (כָּלַם);
disgrace
KJV: confusion, dishonour, reproach, shame.

H3641.definition:
or כַּלְנֵה; also כַּלְנוֹ; of foreign derivation;
Calneh or Calno, a place in the Assyrian empire
KJV: Calneh, Calno. Compare H3656 (כַּנֶּה).

H3642.definition:
a primitive root;
to pine after
KJV: long.

H3643.definition:
from H3642 (כָּמַהּ); pining;
Kimham, an Israelite
KJV: Chimham.

H3644.definition:
or כָּמוֹ; (compare H3651 (כֵּן));
a form of the prefix 'k-', but used separately  as, thus, so
KJV: according to, (such) as (it were, well as), in comparison of, like (as, to, unto), thus, when, worth.

H3645.definition:
or (Jeremiah 48:7) כְּמִישׁ; from an unused root meaning to subdue; the powerful;
Kemosh, the god of the Moabites
KJV: Chemosh.

H3646.definition:
from an unused root meaning to store up or preserve;
'cummin' (from its use as a condiment)
KJV: cummin.

H3647.definition:
a primitive root;
to store away, i.e. (figuratively) in the memory
KJV: lay up in store.

H3648.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to intertwine or contract, i.e. (by implication) to shrivel (as with heat); figuratively, to be deeply affected with passion (love or pity)
KJV: be black, be kindled, yearn.

H3649.definition:
from H3648 (כָּמַר);
properly, an ascetic (as if shrunk with self-maceration), i.e. an idolatrous priest (only in plural)
KJV: Chemarims (idolatrous) priests.

H3650.definition:
redupl. from H3648 (כָּמַר);
obscuration (as if from shrinkage of light, i.e. an eclipse (only in plural)
KJV: blackness.

H3651.definition:
from H3559 (כּוּן);
properly, set upright; hence (figuratively as adjective) just; but usually (as adverb or conjunction) rightly or so (in various applications to manner, time and relation; often with other particles)
KJV: [phrase] after that (this, -ward, -wards), as... as, [phrase] (for-) asmuch as yet, [phrase] be (for which) cause, [phrase] following, howbeit, in (the) like (manner, -wise), [idiom] the more, right, (even) so, state, straightway, such (thing), surely, [phrase] there (where) -fore, this, thus, true, well, [idiom] you.

H3652.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3651 (כֵּן);
so
KJV: thus.

H3653.definition:
the same as H3651 (כֵּן), used as a noun;
a stand, i.e. pedestal or station
KJV: base, estate, foot, office, place, well.

H3654.definition:
from H3661 (כָּנַן) in the sense of fastening; (from infixing its sting; used only in plural (and irregular in Exodus 8:17,18; Hebrews 13:14))
a gnat
KJV: lice, [idiom] manner.

H3655.definition:
a primitive root;
to address by an additional name; hence, to eulogize
KJV: give flattering titles, surname (himself).

H3656.definition:
for H3641 (כַּלְנֶה);
Canneh, a place in Assyria
KJV: Canneh.

H3657.definition:
from H3661 (כָּנַן);
a plant (as set)
KJV: [idiom] vineyard.

H3658.definition:
from a unused root meaning to twang;
a harp
KJV: harp.

H3659.definition:
for H3204 (יְכׇנְיָה);
Conjah, an Israelite king
KJV: Coniah.

H3660.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3644 (כְּמוֹ);
so or thus
KJV: so, (in) this manner (sort), thus.

H3661.definition:
a primitive root;
to set out, i.e. plant
KJV: [idiom] vineyard.

H3662.definition:
from H3661 (כָּנַן); planted;
Kenani, an Israelite
KJV: Chenani.

H3663.definition:
or כְּנַנְיָהוּ; from H3661 (כָּנַן) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has planted;
Kenanjah, an Israelite
KJV: Chenaniah.

H3664.definition:
a primitive root;
to collect; hence, to enfold
KJV: gather (together), heap up, wrap self.

H3665.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to bend the knee; hence, to humiliate, vanquish
KJV: bring down (low), into subjection, under, humble (self), subdue.

H3666.definition:
from H3665 (כָּנַע) in the sense of folding (compare H3664 (כָּנַס));
a package
KJV: wares.

H3667.definition:
from H3665 (כָּנַע); humiliated;
Kenaan, a son a Ham; also the country inhabited by him
KJV: Canaan, merchant, traffick.

H3668.definition:
feminine of H3667 (כְּנַעַן);
Kenaanah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Chenaanah.

H3669.definition:
patrial from H3667 (כְּנַעַן);
a Kenaanite or inhabitant of Kenaan; by implication, a pedlar (the Canaanites standing for their neighbors the Ishmaelites, who conducted mercantile caravans)
KJV: Canaanite, merchant, trafficker.

H3670.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to project laterally, i.e. probably (reflexive) to withdraw
KJV: be removed.

H3671.definition:
from H3670 (כָּנַף);
an edge or extremity; specifically (of a bird or army) a wing, (of a garment or bedclothing) a flap, (of the earth) a quarter, (of a building) a pinnacle
KJV: [phrase] bird, border, corner, end, feather(-ed), [idiom] flying, [phrase] (one an-) other, overspreading, [idiom] quarters, skirt, [idiom] sort, uttermost part, wing(-ed).

H3672.definition:
or כִּנֶּרֶתlemma כִּנֶרֶת missing dagesh, corrected to כִּנֶּרֶת; respectively plural and singular feminine from the same as H3658 (כִּנּוֹר); perhaps harp-shaped;
Kinneroth or Kinnereth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chinnereth, Chinneroth, Cinneroth.

H3673.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3664 (כָּנַס);
to assemble
KJV: gather together.

H3674.definition:
from H3655 (כָּנָה);
a colleague (as having the same title)
KJV: companion.

H3675.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3674 (כְּנָת)
{a colleague (as having the same title)}
KJV: companion.

H3676.definition:
apparently a contraction for H3678 (כִּסֵּא), but probably by erroneous transcription for H5251 (נֵס)
{a flag; also a sail; by implication, a flagstaff; generally a signal; figuratively, a token}
KJV: sworn.

H3677.definition:
or כֶּסֶה; apparently from H3680 (כָּסָה);
properly, fulness or the full moon, i.e. its festival
KJV: (time) appointed.

H3678.definition:
or כִּסֵּה; from H3680 (כָּסָה);
properly, covered, i.e. a throne (as canopied)
KJV: seat, stool, throne.

H3679.definition:
for H3778 (כַּשְׂדִּי)
{a Kasdite, or descendant of Kesed; by implication, a Chaldaean (as if so descended); also an astrologer (as if proverbial of that people}
KJV: Chaldean.

H3680.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to plump, i.e. fill up hollows; by implication, to cover (for clothing or secrecy)
KJV: clad self, close, clothe, conceal, cover (self), (flee to) hide, overwhelm. Compare H3780 (כָּשָׂה).

H3681.definition:
passive participle of H3680 (כָּסָה);
properly, covered, i.e. (as noun) a covering
KJV: covering.

H3682.definition:
from H3680 (כָּסָה);
a cover (garment); figuratively, a veiling
KJV: covering, raiment, vesture.

H3683.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut off
KJV: cut down (up).

H3684.definition:
from H3688 (כָּסַל);
properly, fat, i.e. (figuratively) stupid or silly
KJV: fool(-ish).

H3685.definition:
the same as H3684 (כְּסִיל);
any notable constellation; specifically Orion (as if a burly one)
KJV: constellation, Orion.

H3686.definition:
the same as H3684 (כְּסִיל);
Kesil, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chesil.

H3688.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be fat, i.e. (figuratively) silly
KJV: be foolish.

H3689.definition:
from H3688 (כָּסַל);
properly, fatness, i.e. by implication (literally) the loin (as the seat of the leaf fat) or (generally) the viscera; also (figuratively) silliness or (in a good sense) trust
KJV: confidence, flank, folly, hope, loin.

H3690.definition:
feminine of H3689 (כֶּסֶל);
in a good sense, trust; in a bad one, silliness
KJV: confidence, folly.

H3691.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
Kisleu, the 9th Hebrew month
KJV: Chisleu.

H3692.definition:
from H3688 (כָּסַל); hopeful;
Kislon, an Israelite
KJV: Chislon.

H3693.definition:
from H3688 (כָּסַל); fertile;
Kesalon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chesalon.

H3694.definition:
feminine plural of passive participle of H3688 (כָּסַל); fattened;
Kesulloth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chesulloth.

H3695.definition:
a plural probably of foreign derivation;
Casluchim, a people cognate to the Egyptians
KJV: Casluhim.

H3696.definition:
from the feminine plural of H3689 (כֶּסֶל) and H8396 (תָּבוֹר); flanks of Tabor;
Kisloth-Tabor, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chisloth-tabor.

H3697.definition:
a primitive root;
to shear
KJV: [idiom] only, poll. Compare H3765 (כִּרְסֵם).

H3698.definition:
from H3697 (כָּסַם);
spelt (from its bristliness as if just shorn)
KJV: fitches, rie.

H3699.definition:
a primitive root;
to estimate
KJV: make count.
